# Lines NoWayOS's tools/pi-run must see from the showcase's tour on the Pi 5,
# in this order, as whole serial lines: the run's start -
# its watchdog PD watching no PD, the ticker asking for 300 s - then every
# line systems/rpi5b_2gb/showcase.expect checks before the launcher's first
# line (the display PD and both USB host PDs), then every line of
# systems/showcase.expect, as the whole of systems/showcase.qmp plays: the
# visitor sign-in twice, the Service desk four times, the pump twice, "Why is this
# secure?" and the attract loop. The Pi keeps its own timings where QEMU's
# image shortens them: the idle warning after 15 s and the reset after 30 s,
# and each confirmation's countdown from 10, whose first tick draws two
# digits' slot alone and the next one digit's. Last, the ticker's end, 300 s
# after go, which resets the board into U-Boot's prompt. Taken from a board
# run's log and checked against QEMU's lines one by one: every line of
# QEMU's is here, its timings the Pi's. A test in
# showcase/showcase-app (tests/tour.rs) keeps every line of the
# showcase's own board run here.
NOWAYOS: watchdog: watching no PD: the PM watchdog is serviced on every tick, for 6 s, for as long as the ticks come
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: ticker: a tick to the watchdog every 2000 ms for the run length, 300 s
NOWAYOS: display-stub: showing each frame on the board's 1920x1080 r5g6b5 framebuffer at its own pixels, from row 0
